## Add Spark SPARQL capability validator

Context:
Task 1 of the Spark SPARQL fail-closed implementation for issue #167 required a
new capability validator that rejects unsupported SPARQL constructs before
translation. The change was developed with strict TDD: a new validator test
suite was added first, observed failing at import time, then minimal production
code was implemented to satisfy the required accepted and rejected constructs.

Changes:

1. src/back/core/w3c/sparql/SparqlCapabilityValidator.py
   Added a fail-closed SPARQL algebra validator using rdflib `prepareQuery`,
   explicit unsupported-feature labels, filter-expression shape checks, path
   rejection, and union branch restrictions.
2. tests/back/core/w3c/sparql/test_sparql_capability_validator.py
   Added unit tests covering valid basic SELECT, invalid syntax handling, and
   rejection of GROUP BY, ORDER BY, numeric FILTER, property paths, subquery,
   MINUS, VALUES, SERVICE, GRAPH, arbitrary UNION, non-literal BIND, and OFFSET.

Modified files:
- src/back/core/w3c/sparql/SparqlCapabilityValidator.py
- tests/back/core/w3c/sparql/test_sparql_capability_validator.py

Tests: uv run --frozen pytest -q -m "not scenario" -> 5874 passed, 304 skipped, 6 deselected in 48.36s
